I hope this is the right place to ask the following question (I would ask this in a beginner chat room but I could not find one).

I would like to save derived SI units, such as ohm, m/s or m/s^2 as string in a database together with a f64 value and found the crate whippyunits which at least seems like it could be capable of doing so. Unfortunately I cannot wrap my head around how to do that. In the documentation the unit expression always seems to be a TokenStream (I believe from the proc_macro2 crate?). How can I transform a string to that or is there something else? I am becoming desperate not knowing how to being able to do that. In the end I would like to do something like the `whippyunits::quantity!(500.0, mm)` (https://docs.rs/whippyunits/latest/whippyunits/macro.quantity.html) does just with the second argument (the `unit_expr`) being a string. Any ideas or suggestions?
